<?php
/**
 * ============================================================================
 * OPTIONAL — ONLY for a SECTION-LIKE (container) element.
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * NOTE THE `.example` SUFFIX. This file is deliberately NOT loadable. The
 * loader looks for `class-fw-shortcode-{folder-name}.php`, and if that file
 * exists but does not define the matching class it emits a PHP warning on
 * every page load. Drop the `.example` only when you have actually filled it
 * in, and rename the file to match your folder:
 *
 *     class-fw-shortcode-{your-folder-name}.php
 *
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * DO YOU NEED THIS FILE?
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * NO — for a LEAF element (a heading, a button, a slider, a card, a gallery:
 * anything that renders content and holds no builder rows). A leaf needs only
 * config.php + options.php + views/view.php (+ static.php + static/). The
 * loader auto-discovers the folder; there is nothing to register. This is the
 * overwhelmingly common case, and it is what the rest of this template is.
 *
 * YES — for a SECTION-LIKE element: one that lives at the ROOT of the page
 * and HOLDS rows and columns, behaving like the built-in `[section]`. Wiring
 * it makes the element automatically participate in the section sorter,
 * Save-as-Template, section export/import, the items corrector, and full-page
 * templates.
 *
 * You write only files inside your own folder. Everything discovers the type
 * through the hooks below.
 *
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * SUBSTITUTIONS
 *   {your_type}   snake_case tag — the FOLDER NAME with dashes turned into
 *                 underscores. A folder `hero-banner` is the tag `hero_banner`.
 *   {YourType}    Studly_Case fragment for the class name (Hero_Banner)
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * Everything below is commented out. Uncomment, substitute, rename the file.
 */

