/**
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * WHAT YOU DO **NOT** WRITE FOR A SECTION-LIKE ELEMENT
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * All of this is auto-wired by the two hooks above. Touching any of it is a
 * sign you have gone off the path:
 *
 *   · the section-like registry, the section-like factory view, the item
 *     corrector, the section sorter, the templates feature
 *   · a save-as-template button, a sort-sections row, import/export handling,
 *     hierarchy validation
 *   · registering the page-builder item's CSS/JS — the parent class
 *     auto-locates includes/page-builder-{your_type}-item/static/{css,js}/
 *   · ANY file outside your own folder
 *
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * OTHER PITFALLS
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * · Shortcode tag != item type. By default the item class's
 *   get_shortcode_slug() returns get_type(). Override it in the item class
 *   only in the rare case they differ.
 * · Stay self-contained. Copying a pattern from another element is fine;
 *   `require`-ing PHP from another element's folder at runtime creates
 *   load-order coupling. Shared helpers belong in the extension's includes/.
 * · view.php receives `$content` — the rendered inner rows/columns. Echo it
 *   inside your wrapper, or the element swallows everything the user puts in
 *   it.
 */
